  ],
  "engine": "std",
  "mode": "latin",
  "compose": [
    "modern"
  ],
  "source": "ANSI Dvorak Simplified Keyboard layout; key ids are US-QWERTY physical positions named by their unshifted character (docs/SPEC-SCHEMA.md 'Key ids'). Each key id maps to the character that physical key produces in Dvorak.",
  "x-notes": {
    "why": "SPEC-MODES ReqMode2 requires an English mode that selects qwerty/dvorak/colemak. This adds Dvorak as a selectable Latin layout.",
    "composition": "There is none, by design. A literal value is not a jamo, so process_jamo() takes the ic.c:170 branch and commits it directly, leaving the buffer empty. That is what makes ReqMode6's 'commit per character' fall out rather than be special-cased.",
    "not_a_layout_choice": "This is a data addition required to measure ReqMode8, not a decision to ship dvorak as the English mode. The maintainer decides which Latin layouts English mode offers."
  },
